            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kathy McBee Miller"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So cute! I went to a cooking class that recommended dipping fruit in lemon/lime soda to keep it from turning brown. A good alternative to using lemon juice. Sugar free soda can be used for those watching sugar/weight."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Michelle Suarez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a bit hit at our Halloween party. I put Caramel sauce in the mouths but it just wound up melting off. I suggest a caramel dip in the center instead. Also, use a paring knife to scour where the teeth should go! It makes using slivered almonds so much easier. I almost went insane when I could poke them through.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-24T09:48:01.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hannah Griffy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made these and they were amazing! My cousins all have nut allergies, and I used whole Pumpkin seeds, aswell! So Good!",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-09T02:49:39.013Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AmyLee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy crowd-pleaser for halloween parties. I dipped the slivered almonds in caramel apple dip before inserting them in the apples - it made the almonds stick better, and made the \"teeth\" look even more like a monster mouth with \"gross\" brown stuff around them. Almost didn't make it out of my kitchen to the party because my kids couldn't stop snacking.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-17T11:43:06.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "loddiecheftress"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I soak the apple wedges with OJ &amp; lemon juice. The OJ gives them a wonderful flavor that kids really like (adult to!)",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-23T04:45:20.957Z"
          },
          {
